{%- comment -%}
  PG Page Wide: let the Contact page use the whole screen.

  pg-page-style centres the content column and caps it:

      html body #content > *{ max-width:1000px; margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto }
      html body #content   { padding:52px 20px 76px !important }

  On a wide monitor that leaves the page as a narrow strip with dark emptiness
  either side. The cap is raised to 1280px and the side gutters scale with the
  viewport, so the card uses far more of the screen while still reading as a
  deliberate centred panel.

  NOT edge to edge, which is where this landed first. With no cap at all the
  card simply became the viewport: the two form columns stretched to ~700px
  each, the labels sat a screen apart from their fields, and the whole thing
  stopped looking like a box at all. A cap is what makes centring meaningful --
  auto margins have nothing to distribute once an element fills its container.
  1280px is wide enough to fix the narrow-strip problem and narrow enough that
  the form still reads as one object.

  Two details make this land without touching pg-page-style itself:

  - The 1000px cap carries NO !important, so a plain !important override beats
    it regardless of load order. That matters, because this renders from
    pg-cart-fast (4th in footer-group) while pg-page-style is 21st and would
    otherwise win every tie.
  - The padding DOES carry !important, so that one needs a doubled id to
    out-specify it.

  MOBILE IS DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED. pg-page-style already narrows the gutters
  to 14px under 600px, and that rule is what keeps the form usable on a phone.
  Every change here is inside a min-width:601px query, so the phone layout is
  bit-for-bit what it was.

  Gated on the page handle in Liquid, exactly as pg-page-style is, so this
  cannot reach the product pages, the cart, or anything else.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pgw_h = page.handle | default: '' -%}
{%- if pgw_h == 'contact' or pgw_h == 'track-order' or pgw_h == 'track-your-order' -%}
<style>
  html body #content > *{
    max-width:1280px !important;
    margin-left:auto !important;
    margin-right:auto !important;
  }

  @media (min-width:601px){
    html body #content#content{
      padding-left:clamp(20px,4vw,72px) !important;
      padding-right:clamp(20px,4vw,72px) !important;
    }
  }
</style>
{%- endif -%}
